# ATACseq conda environments

Makefile and definitions for the `ATACseq_R` and `ATACseq_Tools` conda
environments.

`ATACseq_R` is R 4.6 plus the compiler toolchain and system libraries. The R
packages in `PackagesToInstall.txt` are installed from source with BiocManager,
because there are no conda builds for R 4.6 yet. The build scripts and recipes
are shared with the other environments. They live in `../R_build_common/`
(see the README there).

## Files

1. `Makefile`: environment-specific targets (run `make help`).
1. `ATACseq_R.yaml`, `ATACseq_Tools.yaml`: conda environment definitions.
1. `PackagesToInstall.txt`: CRAN/Bioconductor/GitHub R packages to install.

## Usage

```bash
make            # everything
make create-r   # R environment and R package steps only
make help       # list targets
```

`make` runs `create-env`, `create-tools-env`, `fix-cxx-standard`,
`bootstrap-packages`, `update-packages`, `install-packages` and `check-logs`.
If `check-logs` finds a `FAILURE` it exits with an error and keeps
`AllPackageInstallationLogs/` and `AllPackageInstallationSummary.log` for
review. Otherwise the logs are removed.
